  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n   Central idea: We aim to improve the given 70-point Erds minimum overlap solution by optimizing a 140-point step function using gradient-based optimization with carefully designed repair mechanisms. The optimization focuses on minimizing C5 while maintaining integral=1 and bounds within [0,1]. This multiplies the grid size without interpolation, enabling higher resolution exploration.\n   Key components: \n   - 140-point grid for higher resolution\n   - Integrality constraint adjusted by scaling\n   - Gradient descent with finite differences\n   - Feasibility repair using line search and normalization\n   - Target C5 reduction from 0.3808 to lower value\n   Challenges: Non-convex optimization, constraint-compliance, and local optimum avoidance are addressed through tailored line search and repair procedures.\n   2. Mathematical specification\n   - Variables: h \u2208 [0,1]^{140} with \u2211h_i = 70\n   - Objective: C5 = max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx = max_k (autocorrelation calculation with dx=2/140)\n   - Constraints: 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1, \u2211h_i = 70\n   - Repair: Automatic satisfaction except possibly for lower bound clipping. For integral repair, resampling from parent distribution ensures recovery.\n   - representation: 140-point grid [0,2].dx=2/140\n   3. Implementation procedure\n   - validate initial: Use parent's resampled version if available\n   - interpolation: Adaptive resampling for grid transfer from parent\n   - optimization: Gradient descent for entire vector with finite-difference gradient\n   - repair: Integral = 70 (expected) verified by recomposition\n   - termination: Fixed budget for balance between iterations and evaluations\n   4. Search choices and useful variations\n   - Default grid: 140 points\n   - Starting point: If parent initialized, use after resampling\n   - Optimization type: Pure local optimization\n   - Repair callback: Post-tick adjustment ensuring constraints\n   - Simulated annealing: Not included due to time\n   5. Compute budget and robustness\n   - Time: 1300s fixed budget per run\n   - Max evaluate views: 1000 with early termination\n   - Checks: Final candidate still satisfies integral and bounds\n   - Fallback: Resampling parent configuration reused for recovery",
